UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 6, Lesson 1: Steady beat and rhythm', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"The beat is the steady pulse in music, like a heartbeat or a clock ticking. It stays the same while the melody changes. The rhythm is the pattern of long and short sounds that fits over the beat. A quarter note, said ''ta'', lasts one beat, a pair of eighth notes, said ''ti-ti'', share one beat and a quarter rest, a silent beat, is shown with a small symbol. You can tap the beat and clap the rhythm of a song at the same time to hear the difference.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same arts idea to a new artwork or performance, then compare two choices for clarity of effect.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nSay the words ''pizza and pasta'' while tapping a steady beat. Which words fall on one beat each, and which words share a beat?\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: ''Piz-za and pas-ta: piz-za (ti-ti) share one beat, and (ta) takes one beat, then pas-ta (ti-ti).'' So the rhythm is ti-ti ta ti-ti, over a steady beat. The beat stays even while the words make the rhythm.\n\nWATCH FOR\nThinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing. The beat is the steady pulse that does not change, and the rhythm is the pattern of long and short sounds that fits over it.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nChoose three favourite songs or rhymes. Tap the beat gently and clap the rhythm of a line from each, then write the rhythm as ta and ti-ti. Teach one rhythm to someone at home. Sit or stand, whichever is comfortable, and keep the volume low.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one artistic choice you changed and why. Movement or instrument work is optional, adult-supervised and can be described instead.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Creative Arts","learning_intention":"The beat is the steady pulse in music, like a heartbeat or a clock ticking. It stays the same while the melody changes. The rhythm is the pattern of long and short sounds that fits over the beat. A quarter note, said ''ta'', lasts one beat, a pair of eighth notes, said ''ti-ti'', share one beat and a quarter rest, a silent beat, is shown with a small symbol. You can tap the beat and clap the rhythm of a song at the same time to hear the difference.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Explore and learn","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: scrap paper, crayons, safe classroom instruments or clear movement space with an adult nearby"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["CA2-MUS-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Choose three favourite songs or rhymes. Tap the beat gently and clap the rhythm of a line from each, then write the rhythm as ta and ti-ti. Teach one rhythm to someone at home. Sit or stand, whichever is comfortable, and Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using a steady beat on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: Thinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing.. Correction: Strong answer: ''Piz-za and pas-ta: piz-za (ti-ti) share one beat, and (ta) takes one beat, then pas-ta (ti-ti).'' So the. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Thinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing. The beat is the steady pulse that does not change, and the rhythm is the pattern of long and short sounds that fits over it. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating a steady beat on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with a steady beat, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about a steady beat with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for a steady beat. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for a steady beat. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material.","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson.","''Piz-za and pas-ta: piz-za (ti-ti) share one beat, and (ta) takes one beat, then pas-ta (ti-ti).'' So the rhythm is","Thinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing."],"question":"Say the words ''pizza and pasta'' while tapping a steady beat. Which words fall on one beat each, and which words share a beat?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for a steady beat; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["''Piz-za and pas-ta: piz-za (ti-ti) share one beat, and (ta) takes one beat, then pas-ta (ti-ti).'' So the rhythm is","Careful use of a rhythm and explain why it matters with clear evidence.","Thinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing.","The beat is the steady pulse in music, like a heartbeat or a clock ticking."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with a steady beat?","type":"multipl