that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Copy another artwork’s sacred design without permission or guidance.","Example: in ''Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star'' the beat is steady taps while the words are clapped."],"question":"Using this lesson idea — The beat is the steady pulse in music, like a heartbeat or a clock ticking. — which choice is best?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Accuracy means checking evidence and honouring limits or protocols. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Name the artistic choice, its effect, and keep cultural protocols respectful.","Invent missing details to make the answer sound complete.","Ignore safety or cultural protocols to finish faster.","Treat every claim as equally reliable without checking a source or cue."],"question":"Which action keeps elements, techniques and audience effect accurate for a steady beat?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Independence requires a new example that still uses the taught skill. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Name a rhythm and explain why it matters only, with no linked example.","Choose three favourite songs or rhymes.","Retype the worked example with no new example.","Thinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing."],"question":"Which independent response best applies a steady beat to new material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about a steady beat with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating a steady beat on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using a steady beat on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for a steady beat. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with a steady beat, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: Thinking that the beat and the rhythm are the same thing.. Correction: Strong answer: ''Piz-za and pas-ta: piz-za (ti-ti) share one beat, and (ta) takes one beat, then pas-ta (ti-ti).'' So the. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent artwork or performance notes and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-arts-y3-w06-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA Creative Arts alignment using catalogue outcome codes (CA2-*); content-point mapping remains pending. First Nations arts content requires local Aboriginal educator or Custodian guidance before acceptance; do not invent sacred designs.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise a steady beat.","Read the mission before you start making or performing.","Keep the audience effect of your choice in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reasons with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not name an effect clearly."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the element or technique that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore elements, safety or respectful practice.","Prefer a named artistic reason over